# General Rules

Prefer the smallest change that completes the request. Do not reformat, refactor, or restyle unrelated code.

## Scope

- Edit only the files and lines needed for the task.
- Do not create extra files, folders, docs, tests, or configs unless the user asked or the change cannot work without them.
- Do not delete or rename files as a side effect.
- Do not "clean up while you're here": no drive-by refactors, unused-import sweeps, comment rewrites, or style pass over the whole file.

## When adding code

- Reuse existing helpers, types, and patterns instead of introducing new abstractions.
- Add comments only when the logic is non-obvious; never narrate the diff.
- If a larger cleanup would help, mention it in the reply — do not apply it unasked.

```text
BAD: rewrite a whole module to add one function; reformat imports; add README + extra util file
GOOD: add the function next to its callers, same style, no other files
```
